{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427247-question-concerning-gods-and-monsters-and-familairs-with-dots-less-than-3","id":1427247,"title":"Question concerning Gods and Monsters and Familairs with dots less than 3.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-03T22:52:53-08:00","id":1427247,"title":"Question concerning Gods and Monsters and Familairs with dots less than 3.","content":"Am I missing something?<br /> <br /> The M20 book doesn't really mention Familiar creation, just how much paradox/quintessance, and RP guidelines.<br /> <br /> Gods and monsters does mention a 25 freebie point familiar costing 3 background dots (and 3 quintessance/wk)<br /> <br /> But it also mentions 10 freebies per dot as an example.... the math doesn't add up, so I'm not sure if the section means.... you MUST set 3 dots for a Gods and Monsters Familiar, disregard the book if you set the background dots otherwise.<br /> <br /> Also, AFAIK unless you have very high levels of prime, you need a very high level personal node and avatar to afford a familiar beyond even 1 dot. (Unless I'm mistaken).<br /> <br /> So, how does a 1 dot familiar work? (Do I have to bother even stating it? I could just assume 1 dot means it aint rolling ever, and outside of paradox soak/quintessance cost it has no relevant mechanics)<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18512-uriel","name":"uriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T05:33:29-08:00","id":1427264,"title":"","content":"Lol you want M20 to make sense....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T05:57:39-08:00","id":1427266,"title":"","content":"Worse...he want's <i>familiar </i>rules to make sense :P<br /> Here we don't <i>do</i> that.<br /> <br /> Now, jokes aside. I do remember Gods&amp;Monsters familiar rules being a mess<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>uriel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods and monsters does mention a 25 freebie point familiar costing 3 background dots (and 3 quintessance/wk). But it also mentions 10 freebies per dot as an example.... the math doesn't add up, so I'm not sure if the section means.... you MUST set 3 dots for a Gods and Monsters Familiar, disregard the book if you set the background dots otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, knowing how Mage rolls, I would say that it costs 3 because it's higher than 20 but lower than 30, and you can't have half a point. So it rounds up. A 35 freebie would cost 4 dots and 4 Q/w, a 15 freebie would cost 2 dots and 2 Q/w<br /> <br /> So, you get 10 freebies per dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, AFAIK unless you have very high levels of prime, you need a very high level personal node and avatar to afford a familiar beyond even 1 dot. (Unless I'm mistaken). </div> </div> </div>That depends a bit on the ST because the potency and scarcity of Nodes it's a setting choice. Still, yeah, having a powerful Node would be a very good investment if you want a powerful Familiar<br /> <br /> Having Prime would be good too. Even at 1 it allows to detect Quintessence sources to feed your familiar, and consume your HP to gain Quint if you're in a pinch.<br /> <br /> Avatar wouldn't be necessary, that would just allow you to feed it faster - and I don't think you need to give all the Quint in one shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-04-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T21:00:42-08:00","id":1427328,"title":"","content":"May I recommend <i>Forged by Dragon's Fire</i>? It treats familiars practically like playable characters with regard to how deep and robust their creation goes -- it might prove a good companion to your reading of <i>Gods and Monsters</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}